   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s commitment to the UN Trade and Development (UNCTAD) E-Commerce and Digital Economy Programme in the Pacific supported the development and launch of Fiji&#x2019;s National E-commerce Strategy. The Strategy, developed in partnership with the Fiji Ministry of Trade and the Pacific Digital Economy Programme, built on findings from Fiji&#x2019;s National E-commerce Assessment (2020), led by the Pacific Islands Forum Secretariat. It aligns with the Pacific Regional E-commerce Strategy and Roadmap, endorsed by the Pacific Forum Trade Ministers in 2021. The Strategy identified short-, medium-, and long-term priorities to modernise Fiji&#x2019;s trade systems, foster innovation, and support a dynamic and competitive economy by leveraging e-commerce and digital trade. It aims to expand regional and global market access for Fijian businesses, especially micro, small, and medium enterprises, and enhance export competitiveness through digital trade. At the Strategy&apos;s launch in Suva in February 2025, the Hon Manoa Kamikamica, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister for Trade said &#x2018;Fiji has the potential to develop strong competitive advantages in the e-commerce sector, with its digitally savvy population and growing enthusiasm for new technologies, creating a strong foundation for rapid growth and competitive advantage&#x2019;.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s commitment to the UN Trade and Development (UNCTAD) E-Commerce and Digital Economy Programme supported delivery of capacity building and peer-to-peer learning under UNCTAD&apos;s eTrade for Women Initiative. It delivered a Masterclass for women digital entrepreneurs from South Asia, which built capacity among participants in digital marketing, intellectual property, and fundraising, positioning participants to engage more effectively in global and regional e-commerce and digital trade. The Masterclass enhanced access to networks and encouraged knowledge sharing around inclusive growth and digital transformation. There were 21 participants &#x2013; from Bhutan (3), India (8), Nepal (3) and Sri Lanka (7) &#x2013; who learnt from UNCTAD, each other, and leading regional digital trade experts. Along with fellow alumni, participants also gained access to the eTrade for Women Academy, an online learning hub designed to cultivate new businesses and leadership skills.</narrative>
    </description>
